-- title:
--   Archimedean discrepancy of twisted and standard weighted orbital integrals
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ and $L$ are number fields with $L$ an extension of $K$, $\iota\colon K\to \mathbb{A}_K$ denotes the structure map into the adele ring $\mathbb{A}_K=$ `AdeleRing (𝓞 K) K`, and for $u\in K^\times$ and an idele unit $z$ the element
--   $$\gamma(u,z)\;=\;\mathrm{scalar}(z)\cdot \mathrm{diag}(\iota u,1)\ \in\ \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$$
--   is written for [`AutomorphicForm.centralScalar (𝓞 K) K z * diagUnits2 (Units.map ι u) 1`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L18); its archimedean and finite parts are $\mathrm{glArch}\,\gamma(u,z)\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)$ and $\mathrm{glFin}\,\gamma(u,z)$, with $v$-component $\mathrm{finComponent}_v$ for $v$ in the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_K$. Here $K_\infty$ is the infinite adele ring of $K$, and on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of any topological ring, and on the relevant centralisers, the Borel $\sigma$-algebra generated by the topology is used.
--
--   The data on the $K$-side are: a Haar measure $\nu_{Z,K}$ on $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$; an archimedean test factor $f_{a,K}\colon\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)\to\mathbb{C}$, the hypothesis `hfaK` asserting that $f_{a,K}(g)=\Phi(\mathrm{archEntries}_K g)$ for some $C^\infty$ function $\Phi$ on matrices over the mixed space of $K$ and that $f_{a,K}$ has compact support; a measure $\nu_A$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)$; a constant $c_{\tau K}>0$; for each $u,z$ a measure $\tau_G(u,z)$ on the centraliser of $\gamma(u,z)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, Haar whenever $u\neq 1$ (`hτG`) and satisfying the torus-parametrisation identity `hτGc`: for $u\neq 1$ and every $g$, $\int_{\mathrm{Cent}(\gamma(u,z))} g(t)\,d\tau_G(u,z) = c_{\tau K}\int_{(\mathbb{A}_K^\times)^2} g(\mathrm{diag}(p_1,p_2))\,d(\nu_{Z,K}\times\nu_{Z,K})$; for each $u,z$ a measure $\tau_A(u,z)$ on the centraliser of $\mathrm{glArch}\,\gamma(u,z)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)$, Haar for $u\neq 1$ (`hτA`); for each $u,z,v$ a measure $\tau_F(u,z,v)$ on the local centraliser of $\mathrm{finComponent}_v(\mathrm{glFin}\,\gamma(u,z))$, Haar for $u\neq 1$ (`hτF`) and, again for $u\neq 1$, giving mass $1$ to the preimage of the local integral set $\{g : g$ and $g^{-1}$ have entries in $\mathcal{O}_v\}$ (`hτF1`); and a constant $c_T>0$ together with the factorisation hypothesis `hT`: for $u\neq 1$, a finite set $S$ of finite places and functions $W$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, $W_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)$, $W_S(v)$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ which are almost everywhere strongly measurable for $\tau_A(u,z)$ resp. $\tau_F(u,z,v)$ ($v\in S$), such that $W(t)=W_a(\mathrm{glArch}\,t)\prod_{v\in S}W_S(v)(\mathrm{finComponent}_v(\mathrm{glFin}\,t))$ for every $t$ in the centraliser of $\gamma(u,z)$ which is integral at all $v\notin S$, and $W(t)=0$ for every such $t$ which fails integrality at some $v\notin S$, one has $\int W\,d\tau_G(u,z)=c_T\left(\int W_a\,d\tau_A(u,z)\right)\prod_{v\in S}\int W_S(v)\,d\tau_F(u,z,v)$.
--
--   The data on the $L$-side are: $L/K$ Galois with an automorphism $\sigma$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (`hgen`), and $[L:K]$ prime (`hprime`); an archimedean test factor $\varphi_a\colon\mathrm{GL}_2(L_\infty)\to\mathbb{C}$ satisfying the same smooth-plus-compact-support condition (`hφa`); the matching hypothesis `hmatchA`, namely `AreMatchingArch K L σ φa faK`, which states for the Haar measures `archHaarL K L` and `archHaarK K` that (i) for all $\delta$ with $N_\sigma\delta=\delta\,\sigma\delta\cdots\sigma^{[L:K]-1}\delta$ regular semisimple, all regular semisimple $\gamma\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)$, all $y$ with $\gamma\mapsto y^{-1}(N_\sigma\delta)y$ under base change, and all Haar measures on the centraliser of $\gamma$ and the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser of $\delta$ which are coupled through $y$, every twisted orbital integral value of $\varphi_a\circ\mathrm{archIdentGL}$ at $\delta$ equals every orbital integral value of $f_{a,K}$ at $\gamma$, and (ii) for regular semisimple $\gamma$ admitting no norm, every orbital integral of $f_{a,K}$ at $\gamma$ vanishes; a measure $\nu_A'$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_\infty)$, with the normalisations $\nu_A=$ `archHaarK K` (`hνA`) and $\nu_A'=$ `archHaarL K L` (`hνA'`).
--
--   The two families of integrals being compared are: $J_A\colon K^\times\times\mathbb{A}_K^\times\to\mathbb{C}$, with `hJA` asserting that for $u\neq 1$ the number $J_A(u,z)$ is a weighted orbital integral of $f_{a,K}$ at $\mathrm{glArch}\,\gamma(u,z)$ with respect to $\nu_A$ and $\tau_A(u,z)$, for the weight $y\mapsto -\log \mathrm{archHeight}_K(y)-\log\mathrm{archHeight}_K(w_\infty y)$ with $w_\infty=\mathrm{glArch}$ of the adelic Weyl element, i.e. $J_A(u,z)=\int f_{a,K}(x^{-1}\gamma x)\,\mathrm{wt}(x)\,s(x)\,d\nu_A$ for some section function $s$ for $\tau_A(u,z)$; a family $\delta_A(u,z)\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_\infty)$ which, for $u\neq 1$ and whenever some $\delta$ is a norm of $\mathrm{glArch}\,\gamma(u,z)$, satisfies $N_\sigma(\delta_A(u,z))=\mathrm{toTensorGL}(\mathrm{glArch}\,\gamma(u,z))$ (`hδA`); measures $\tau_A'(u,z)$ on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser of $\delta_A(u,z)$, Haar for $u\neq 1$ (`hτA'`) and, for $u\neq 1$ and $\mathrm{glArch}\,\gamma(u,z)$ a norm, coupled to $\tau_A(u,z)$ with conjugator $y=1$, i.e. the push-forward of $\tau_A'(u,z)$ under the inclusion equals the push-forward of $\tau_A(u,z)$ under `toTensorGL` (`hτA'c`); and $J_A'\colon K^\times\times\mathbb{A}_K^\times\to\mathbb{C}$ with `hJA'` asserting that for $u\neq 1$ and $\mathrm{glArch}\,\gamma(u,z)$ a norm, $J_A'(u,z)$ is a $\sigma$-twisted weighted orbital integral of $\varphi_a\circ\mathrm{archIdentGL}$ at $\delta_A(u,z)$ with respect to $\nu_A'$ and $\tau_A'(u,z)$, for the weight $y\mapsto -\log\mathrm{archHeight}_L(\mathrm{archIdentGL}\,y)-\log\mathrm{archHeight}_L(w_{L,\infty}\,\mathrm{archIdentGL}\,y)$, and `hJA'0` asserting $J_A'(u,z)=0$ for $u\neq 1$ when $\mathrm{glArch}\,\gamma(u,z)$ is not a norm. (Here $\mathrm{archHeight}_F(g)=\prod_{w\mid\infty}\big(\|\det g_w\|/\mathrm{rowNormSq}(g_w)\big)^{m_w}$ with $m_w=$ `w.mult`.)
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exist a function $B_d$ on $(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\to$ mixed space of $K$, i.e. on pairs of points of the mixed space, and families $C_d,E_d$ of such functions indexed by the infinite places $w$ of $K$, with the following properties.
--
--   First, $B_d$ is $C^\infty$ over $\mathbb{R}$, and so are all $C_d(w)$ and all $E_d(w)$. Second, $B_d$, every $C_d(w)$ and every $E_d(w)$ have compact support. Third, for every pair $p$ of points of the mixed space, if $B_d(p)\neq 0$, or $C_d(w)(p)\neq 0$ or $E_d(w)(p)\neq 0$ for some $w$, then both preimages $(\mathrm{ringEquiv\_mixedSpace}_K)^{-1}(p_0)$ and $(\mathrm{ringEquiv\_mixedSpace}_K)^{-1}(p_1)$ are units of $K_\infty$. Fourth, there is a compact set $C_{aD}\subseteq K_\infty^\times\times K_\infty^\times$ such that every $p$ lying in $\mathrm{tsupport}\,B_d\cup\bigcup_w(\mathrm{tsupport}\,C_d(w)\cup\mathrm{tsupport}\,E_d(w))$ is of the form $p=[\,\mathrm{ringEquiv\_mixedSpace}_K(q_1),\ \mathrm{ringEquiv\_mixedSpace}_K(q_2)\,]$ for some $q=(q_1,q_2)\in C_{aD}$.
--
--   Fifth, writing $N_\infty(u)=\prod_{w\mid\infty}\|(\iota u)_{\infty,w}-1\|^{m_w}$ and, for an infinite place $w$, $a_w(u)=\|\mathrm{archEval}_w(1-(\iota u^{-1})_\infty)\|$ and $b_w(u)=\|\mathrm{archEval}_w((\iota u^{-1})_\infty)\|$, and setting
--   $$p(u,z_S)=\big[\,\mathrm{ringEquiv\_mixedSpace}_K\big((\iota u^{-1})_\infty\big),\ \mathrm{ringEquiv\_mixedSpace}_K\big((z_S\,\iota u)_\infty\big)\,\big],$$
--   for every $u\in K^\times$ with $u\neq 1$ and every idele unit $z_S$ one has
--   $$N_\infty(u)\big(J_A'(u,z_S)-[L:K]\,J_A(u,z_S)\big)\;=\;N_\infty(u)\Big(\prod_{w\mid\infty}\big(a_w(u)/\sqrt{b_w(u)}\big)^{m_w}\Big)^{-1}\Big(B_d(p(u,z_S))+\sum_{w\ \mathrm{real}}a_w(u)\,C_d(w)(p(u,z_S))+\sum_{w\ \mathrm{complex}}a_w(u)^2\log a_w(u)\,E_d(w)(p(u,z_S))\Big),$$
--   the real quantities being regarded as complex numbers and the sums running over the real, respectively complex, infinite places of $K$. The factor $N_\infty(u)$ occurs on both sides of the displayed identity.
--
--   This is the archimedean half of the comparison between $\sigma$-twisted and standard weighted orbital integrals in cyclic base change for $\mathrm{GL}_2$: the discrepancy $J_A'-[L:K]J_A$ at the regular semisimple torus elements $\mathrm{diag}(u,1)$, twisted by a central idele, is expressed through smooth compactly supported functions of the two diagonal entries, with the real places contributing a linear and the complex places a $t^2\log t$ term. It feeds the global window/class-sum comparison [`AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_window_classSum_eq_tsum_mul_tsum_ite_kinkWindow_of_areMatchingArch_of_areMatchingLocal_of_ne_one_unweighted`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_window_classSum_eq_tsum_mul_tsum_ite_kinkWindow_of_areMatchingArch_of_areMatchingLocal_of_ne_one_unweighted).
